rota lap 4458, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; its cardinal seat says run the actual thing rather than read about it, and running it surfaced a red the reading would never have found
think Opened cold: 213 guards, 209 green, 2 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no. Both reds are one fault -- sow_allow_reach on stale projection coverage, and standing_equipment reporting it. Neither is mine; the cure is the full rescrub under Keaton's scrub standfast.
think Water cardinal is foundations/20260823-222019_what-brix-infuse-is.md, and its instruction is to run the census rather than read the sentence about it. tools/c/convergence_census.sh: 12 candidates, 8 proven. One of the four unproven is tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf.sh -- my own lane's writer.
think Ran tools/c/convergence_tree_prove.sh on it. Verdict inert. Then git status showed construction/archive/20260909-999999_itinerary-landed-accounts.md untracked in the LIVE tree. The prover had written into the tree it declares in its own header it never touches.
think Mechanism: the prover cd-s into its pen worktree and then invokes the tool by TOOL_ABS, its absolute path in the real tree. This tree's tools resolve their root from $0 and cd to it, so the subject walks back out of the pen. git grep counted 100 tracked tools carrying that idiom.
think Root cause is the control, not the prover. All five planted operators work on relative paths in the current directory; not one resolves a root from $0. Nineteen checks stood green over a class the pen never held -- the fixed seat's teaching, a stand-in speaking a simpler contract than the answerer.
think Repair: compute the tool's path relative to the repository root, copy the ON-DISK file to that path inside the pen before the baseline is taken, and run that copy. A tool from outside the repository keeps its own path, having no root of this tree's to resolve.
think Re-run then gave refused_on_second, which the prover calls the sharpest divergence. It is not: the shelf writer refuses because a shelf is immutable once written, and the tree it leaves is the tree run one left. That is accrete-never-break, not corruption.
think Added a write_once verdict that asks the tree rather than the exit code. The control's own sour.sh, planted as the sharpest divergence, is one of these; added spoil.sh, which writes again AND refuses, so refused_on_second is exercised by something that earns it.
obs The census reading is unchanged by the repair, because that column reads whether somebody wrote a sibling assertion. Adding one to itinerary_account_shelf_control.sh -- the second run asserted on the BYTES rather than on the refusal message -- moved it 8 to 9 of 12.
obs The pin stood 232 bytes under its bound, so the row could not land until %620 folded to a shelf. That row's lesson already sits on the fleet baton, so the shelf keeps the record where the teaching is not.
obs The send met a spine collision: a peer booked %667 at 20260909.155028 while my row carried 20260909.170804, so the earlier stamp keeps the number and my unshared row renumbered to %668. It cost one line, because every living citation of it -- the card, this log, the commit body -- already spelled the stamp rather than the number. That is derived-spine rule 4 paying for itself on the first firing after I read it.
